---
pagination:
  data: unstrungDocs.documents
  size: 1
  alias: doc
  # So every document's page is in collections.all, which the sitemap lists.
  # Without it only the first page is.
  addAllPagesToCollections: true
permalink: "/unstrung/docs/{{ doc.id }}/"
sidePanel: docs
eleventyComputed:
  title: "{{ doc.title }}"
  description: "{{ doc.title }}, from the unstrung documentation."
  canonical: "{{ '/unstrung/' if doc.id == 'introduction' else '' }}"
---
{#- One page per document in unstrungApp's user-docs, from content/_data/unstrungDocs.js.
    None when the fetched release has no documentation.

    The introduction is also the /unstrung/ page, with the same text and title.
    canonical names /unstrung/ as its main address, which the layout writes as
    a link in the head for search engines. No other document has one.

    The run and download links from unstrung-links.njk come first, straight
    after the h1, as on /unstrung/docs/. They are added here and not written in
    the documents, because the app shows the same documents in its Help menu,
    where the links do not belong. -#}
{% include "unstrung-links.njk" %}
{{ doc.html | safe }}
